{"duration_api_ms":140722,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"e4998be9-4015-4167-ae59-a1b94e58366c","total_cost_usd":0.207128,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16306,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":14190,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":9098},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16306,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":14190,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16306,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16306},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":14190,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":16306,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.207128,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":9098,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"The front is a one-dimensional ridge at the corner D=3.385, bluntness=1.2, cone=70, parameterised by gamma from -1.5 to -3.5702. All three limits pin that corner: g<=12 caps |gamma| near 3.570, mass fraction (proportional to D^2) caps D near 3.3852, and the bluntness/cone hull edge blocks any move to more bluntness or a smaller cone (1.203, 1.21, 1.25 and cone 69 all fail on hull or geometry). Lowering bluntness or cone, or shrinking D, raises flux and T, so those moves are dominated. Normalised hypervolume is 0.3555 and has gained only about 1e-4 to 4e-5 per round since round 4. The remaining gain is in the sparse stretches of the gamma ridge, mainly -2.2 to -2.6 and -2.9 to -3.28, plus tiny D and gamma tweaks at the g and mass-fraction limits.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-948029610632 to C-bc377838462a: flux rises 227k to 275k and T falls 417.9 K to 391.1 K monotonically with steeper gamma, at fixed D=3.385, bluntness 1.2, cone 70.\",\"Ridge gaps: C-2d7e6dba2267 (-2.2: 242.1k, 407.1 K) to C-249a4f21af03 (-2.6: 251.4k, 401.8 K), and C-3f1d8b1bcb6a (-2.9) to C-f9075e31d70a (-3.28). The ridge is convex, so points inside these gaps should enter the front.\",\"Mass fraction margin is 0.0001449 at D=3.385, 8.6e-5 at 3.3851 and 2.7e-5 at 3.3852 (C-0265d5374015, C-8d69d1842e32). It is 0.0497 at D=3.3 (C-6041504dc2c9), which matches the D^2 scaling. The zero crossing is near D=3.38525.\",\"g margin is 5.2e-4 at gamma -3.567 (C-78a9a956afab), 4.7e-5 at -3.57 (C-81e40e27ff03) and 2.5e-5 at -3.5702 (C-bc377838462a). The limit is near -3.5704.\",\"C-956957ec60d4, C-7112b6b29bcf and C-14444dd6b10a (bluntness 1.19, 1.15, 1.1) show lower bluntness raises flux and breaks mass fraction. C-3136d3bd2588, C-3d41ce848a30, C-05edbf22eaa2 and C-7db223121090 show the hull blocks bluntness above 1.2 and cone below 70 at these D.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Peak g is set almost entirely by gamma, which fixes the steep end of the ridge. Mass fraction scales with D^2, which fixes D. A larger D and a blunt 70 degree cone give the lowest ballistic coefficient, so peak heating occurs higher and both flux and T fall. Along gamma, shallower entry lowers flux but lengthens the heat pulse and raises T. That gives a smooth convex trade-off curve. The corner design is already at every bound, so the useful moves are to densify the ridge and to test the D and gamma limits, gaining a little hypervolume without risking rejected slots. The gamma^-0.25 and D^2 scalings are partly from prior knowledge; the numbers here are interpolated from the rows cited.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Predictions are linear or convex interpolations between neighbouring ridge points and should be accurate to about 0.3 K and 1k W/m2. The main risk is the D=3.3852 and gamma -3.5703 points sitting on the mass-fraction and g limits. I estimate margins of about +1e-5 for g and +2.7e-5 for mass fraction, and a small error would make them infeasible. There is no evidence of any better region away from the corner, so I spent no slots on exploration beyond it.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-bc377838462a\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the shallow end of the ridge, between gamma -1.5 and -1.6.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":228220,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":417.05,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Small staircase gap on the front; near-certain feasible.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-bc377838462a\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between -1.65 and -1.85.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.7},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":231220,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":414.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the ridge at D=3.385.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-bc377838462a\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between -1.7 and -1.85.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.75},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":232260,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":413.85,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the ridge at D=3.385.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-bc377838462a\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between -1.85 and -2.0.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.9},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":235420,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":411.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the ridge at D=3.385.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-bc377838462a\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between -1.9 and -2.0.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.95},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":236500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":410.75,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the ridge at D=3.385.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-bc377838462a\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between -2.0 and -2.2.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.1},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":239830,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":408.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the ridge at D=3.385.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-bc377838462a\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the large -2.2 to -2.6 gap, the widest on the front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":244390,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":405.75,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Largest staircase gap; convexity may put the point slightly below the chord.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-bc377838462a\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the large -2.2 to -2.6 gap.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":246710,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":404.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Largest staircase gap on the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-bc377838462a\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the large -2.2 to -2.6 gap.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.45},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":247870,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":403.75,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Largest staircase gap on the front.\",\"requested_fide